## 10. Acceptance Criteria

The feature is complete only when all applicable criteria are proven:

- [ ] Initial and changing network conditions are represented accurately.
- [ ] `navigator.onLine` is treated as a hint, not proof of API/Cloudinary availability.
- [ ] Cloudinary upload is disabled when offline, and the specified warning appears.
- [ ] Cloudinary upload is disabled when SentinelOps API authorization/signature service is unreachable.
- [ ] The existing offline project workflow remains functional.
- [ ] A legitimate authorized user can upload multiple validated images to Cloudinary.
- [ ] Cloudinary credentials and API secrets remain server-side.
- [ ] Project/business authorization and upload limits are enforced server-side.
- [ ] Cloudinary attachment metadata is saved reliably and sync-compatible.
- [ ] Image privacy/access policy is explicitly chosen and documented.
- [ ] Every uploaded project image is named `{ProjectName}_{StartDate}_{Sequence}` with the sequence starting at 1 per project, never reused, stable across retries, and safe against multi-device collisions.
- [ ] Generated names are sanitized, derived from the project's current name and start date, and kept separate from the opaque Cloudinary public ID; legacy attachments are not renamed without approval.
- [ ] Failure, retry, partial success, and interrupted persistence are handled without false success or silent data loss.
- [ ] Automated tests and production build are run where tooling is available.
- [ ] Deployment and environment setup instructions are documented.
- [ ] No existing feature or unrelated architecture was changed without authorization.

Do not mark an acceptance criterion complete without implementation evidence or an executed test.

